.TH TECHNE 1 "2026-10-06" "techne 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&
.PP
techne \- operate Knowledge Islands Techne Harness
.SH SYNOPSIS
\&
.TP
.B techne
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.TP
.B techne completion bash|zsh
Print a completion definition for the selected shell.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&
.B techne
is the operator command-line interface for the Techne controller
execution fabric.
It keeps provider credentials out of command arguments and enforces the
configured AWS account boundary before controller and agent host operations.
.SH COMMANDS
\&
.TP
.B diag
Report share-safe tool/version, local/release/unknown installation mode,
executing host platform and architecture, runtime/version, and effective
configuration presence without network access. Configuration uses defaults,
environment variables, and options rather than a file.
Local identifiers are redacted unless
.B --full
is supplied; review full output before sharing it.
Local provenance requires a resolved development checkout matching this tool's
source/package layout and a Git checkout or worktree marker. Copied source
without that evidence reports unknown; a source URL alone is insufficient.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show general help, or help for a command or command group such as
.BR host .
.TP
.B doctor
Check the local runtime, AWS CLI, Session Manager plugin and expected
AWS identity.
Show the same diagnostic context, read-only scope, healthy/unhealthy verdict,
and pass/warn/fail/skipped counts. Identity may contact AWS but never changes
provider state; unavailable prerequisite checks report actionable failures and
dependent identity checks are explicitly skipped. Numeric account identities
and raw provider errors are omitted. Health does not imply package freshness.
.TP
.B auth login
Reconcile authentication surfaces declared by the effective Techne
configuration with supported provider clients installed locally. The current
configuration declares AWS only. A valid session is retained; a recognised
expired IAM Identity Center session opens an interactive AWS SSO login and
then revalidates the expected account. Missing clients, unsupported profiles
and non-authentication failures do not trigger login.
JSON output and non-interactive terminals are not supported for this command.
.TP
.B controller status
Report the configured controller CloudFormation stack and controller
instance.
.TP
.B controller bootstrap
Open a private interactive Session Manager bootstrap session on the
controller.
JSON output is not supported for this interactive command.
.TP
.B host status
Report the one non-terminated agent host instance tagged
.BR ki-agent-host-id=agent-host ,
its state and region, without changing it.
When the instance is running, also run the harness
.B operations/aws/agent-host/status.sh
from the harness checkout and print its workspace report unchanged;
JSON output carries it in a
.B workspace
object.
A failed workspace report exits 1 after the instance report.
.TP
.B host setup [--pull]
Check that Tailscale reaches the agent host, then run the harness
.B operations/aws/agent-host/setup.sh
from the harness checkout to converge the host workspace over SSH.
.B --pull
fast-forwards clean checkouts on the host.
.TP
.B host start
Start a stopped agent host and wait until it runs.
.TP
.B host stop
Stop a running agent host.
.TP
.B host teardown
Terminate the agent host after the instance identifier is typed at an
interactive prompt. This cannot be undone.
.TP
.B host connect [path]
Check that Tailscale reaches the agent host, then open
.I path
(default home) in Zed over SSH. Makes no AWS call.
.PP
Host commands use the agent-host profile, refuse credentials that are not the
agent-host operator role in the expected account, and refuse unless exactly one
tagged instance exists.
.BR setup ,
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.B teardown
and
.B connect
accept
.BR --dry-run .
The
.B setup
and
.B connect
commands make no AWS call.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh
Print a sourceable Bash or Zsh completion definition to standard output.
The installer does not alter shell startup files or completion directories.
.SH COMPLETION
\&
.PP
For the current Bash session, run
.BR "source <(techne completion bash)" .
For Zsh, write
.B techne completion zsh
to an
.B _techne
file in a directory on
.B fpath
before running
.BR compinit .
Keep persistent activation in shell configuration or a configuration manager.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
\&
.TP
.BI "--profile " name
Select the AWS profile.
.TP
.BI "--region " region
Select the AWS region.
.TP
.BI "--account " id
Set the expected AWS account identifier.
.TP
.BI "--controller-stack " name
Select the controller CloudFormation stack.
.TP
.BI "--host-profile " name
Select the AWS profile for the agent host operator role.
.TP
.BI "--harness-dir " path
Select the local ki-techne-harness checkout whose agent-host scripts
.B host setup
and
.B host status
run. Defaults to
.BR $HOME/workspaces/kit/knowledgeislands/ki-techne-harness .
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print host changes without making them.
.TP
.B --pull
Fast-forward clean checkouts on the host during
.BR "host setup" .
.TP
.B --json
Request machine-readable output where supported.
.TP
.B --full
Include local paths and identifiers in diagnostic output.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show help for the selected command or command group; a command group given
without a command is a usage error.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\&
.TP
.B AWS_PROFILE
Default AWS profile.
.TP
.B AWS_REGION
Default AWS region.
.TP
.B EXPECTED_AWS_ACCOUNT
AWS account safety boundary.
.TP
.B CONTROLLER_STACK_NAME
Default controller stack name.
.TP
.B TECHNE_HOST_PROFILE
Default agent host profile.
.TP
.B TECHNE_HARNESS_DIR
Default ki-techne-harness checkout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\&
.PP
Returns 0 on success, 1 on operational or health-check failure and 2 on
invalid command usage.
.SH SECURITY
\&
.PP
Never place credentials, provider sessions, numeric operator identifiers
or raw Telegram updates in command arguments, Git or retained evidence.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&
.TP
.BR aws (1)
